{
 "encounter_id": "00691",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Morning. I'll be honest, I've got forty minutes before a site meeting, so can we be efficient? It's about my gout, and my kidneys."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "We'll be efficient but thorough, because the two are connected. Tell me about the gout first."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Big toe, left foot, swelled up last week, red and agony. It's gone down now, three days of tablets."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And what did you take for it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Naproxen, 500 mg, twice a day, from the stash I keep. I always have some."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's important. Let's go through everything you take."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Allopurinol, 100 mg once a day. Ramipril, 5 mg once a day. Amlodipine, 5 mg once a day. And atorvastatin, 20 mg at night."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. And your conditions, remind me."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Gout, obviously. Kidney function, the blood tests said it's dropped a bit, chronic kidney disease, they called it. And high blood pressure."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any gout in the family?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My father had it terribly, in his fifties."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 72, blood pressure 144 over 88, temperature 36.6, oxygen 98 percent, weight 94 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is the pressure bad? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A bit above where I'd like, and I'll come back to that. Now let me look at the toe. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Looks normal to me. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The big toe joint is no longer red or swollen, just a little tender.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Told you. So what's the issue? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Here's the thing. Naproxen is an anti-inflammatory, and with kidney disease, and on ramipril, it can damage the kidneys further. I'd like you to stop using it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's the only thing that works for the toe. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There are safer options for a flare, and we'll agree them. For now, keep the naproxen out of the drawer."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. And the allopurinol? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's the right drug for preventing attacks, and the dose is suitable for your kidneys. Keep taking it daily, even when the toe's fine."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I do. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And drink plenty of water, at least two litres, and keep the beer low."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The beer, again. Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's all I need for today. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Good. Thanks. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Mind that toe on the ladders this afternoon. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll wear the proper boots. ~"
  }
 ],
